---
// AI coding agents: SKILL.md and its honest limit (docs/agents.md). The excerpt quotes SKILL.md.
import Section from '../ui/Section.astro';
import Heading from '../ui/Heading.astro';
import Window from '../ui/Window.astro';
import Icon from '../ui/Icon.astro';
---

<Section id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title" inner="agents-grid">
  <div>
    <Heading id="agents-title" eyebrow="Built for AI coding agents" gap={false}>
      Let agents use secrets without handing them over.
      <Fragment slot="lede">
        Add <code>SKILL.md</code> to your agent. It teaches <code>ku run</code> and <code>ku secret list</code>, and what
        never to do: no reveals, no printing values, no values in commands or files.
      </Fragment>
    </Heading>
    <aside class="note" aria-label="Accepted risk">
      <Icon name="info" size={20} />
      <p>
        <b>The honest limit.</b> A command an agent runs can print its own environment. Give agents low-value development
        secrets, mark sensitive ones <code>requires_authorize</code>, and rotate on leak.{' '}
        <a href="/docs/agents/">Read the agent guide</a>
      </p>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <Window title="SKILL.md" chrome="file" data-reveal aria-label="An excerpt of SKILL.md">
    <div class="skill">
      <p class="quote">Secrets live in a vault. You run commands <em>with</em> them; you never read them.</p>
      <p class="h do">Do</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>ku secret list app:shop env:dev</code><span>names, versions and tags, never values</span></li>
        <li><code>ku run env:dev -- npm run dev</code><span>secrets injected as env vars</span></li>
        <li><span>If a secret is blocked or you are not permitted, stop and tell the user.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="h never">Never</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code>ku secret get --reveal</code><span>or <code>--out</code>: they need the user’s own confirmation</span></li>
        <li><span>Print, echo, log or paste a secret value anywhere.</span></li>
        <li><span>Put a value in a command line, a URL, a config file or a test fixture.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <a slot="footer" href="/docs/skill/">The full skill</a>
  </Window>
</Section>

<style>
  :global(.agents-grid) {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .note {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: var(--k-space-6);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--k-line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgba(12, 29, 34, 0.6);
    color: var(--k-muted);
    font-size: var(--k-text-md);
  }
  .note :global(svg) {
    flex: none;
    color: var(--k-amber);
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }
  .note p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .note a {
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* the file's text */
  .skill {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0.25rem;
  }
  .quote {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  }
  em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--k-acc);
  }
  .h {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font: 600 0.8125rem/1 var(--k-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .do {
    color: var(--k-acc);
  }
  .never {
    color: var(--k-ink);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }
  li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--k-muted);
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--k-line);
  }
  li > code {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--k-ink);
    font-size: var(--k-text-sm);
    white-space: normal;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    :global(.agents-grid) {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
